  "data_abstract": "BNL-RHIC. Hard-scattered parton probes produced in collisions of large nuclei indicate large partonic energy loss, possibly with collective produced-medium response to the lost energy. We present measurements of $\\pi^0$ trigger particles at transverse momenta $p^t_T$ = 4\u201312 GeV/$c$ and associated charged hadrons ($p^a_T$ = 0.5\u20137 GeV/$c$) vs. relative azimuthal angle $\\Delta \\phi$ in Au$\\mathord{+}$Au and $p\\mathord{+}p$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV. The Au$\\mathord{+}$Au $\\Delta\\phi$ distribution at low $p^a_T$, whose shape has been interpreted as a medium effect, is modified for $p^t_T$ $<$ 7 GeV/$c$. At higher $p^t_T$, the data are consistent with unmodified or very weakly modified shapes, even for the lowest measured $p^a_T$, which quantitatively challenges some medium response models. The associated yield of hadrons opposing the trigger particle in Au$\\mathord{+}$Au relative to $p\\mathord{+}p$ ($I_{AA}$) is suppressed at high $p_T$ ($I_{AA}$ $\\approx$ 0.35\u20130.5), but less than for inclusive suppression ($R_{AA}$ $\\approx$ 0.2).\n",
